/**
   @page reflow_main The Flow Manager library (reflow)

   reflow sends and receives media for @ref recon_main "recon", and handles
   the NAT traversal and media security for it. It is built on asio and the
   @ref return_main "reTurn client library".

   @section reflow_classes Main Classes
      - flowmanager::FlowManager : Creates media streams, and owns the thread
      that runs all of their asynchronous socket operations. For DTLS-SRTP,
      initializeDtlsFactory() creates the client certificate that every
      stream uses.
      - flowmanager::MediaStream : One media stream, created with
      flowmanager::FlowManager::createMediaStream(). An RTP stream has two
      components, one for RTP and one for RTCP (unless RTCP is disabled), each
      carried by its own flow. The application learns that the stream is
      ready, or has failed, through flowmanager::MediaStreamHandler.
      - flowmanager::Flow : One component of a media stream: a UDP, TCP or
      TLS socket, possibly relayed through a TURN allocation. Its send() and
      receive() functions send and wait for packets, and getLocalTuple(),
      getReflexiveTuple() and getRelayTuple() give the addresses to put in
      SDP.

   @section reflow_nat NAT Traversal
      Each media stream uses one of the flowmanager::MediaStream::NatTraversalMode
      modes:
      - NoNatTraversal : use the local address and port as they are;
      - StunBindDiscovery : learn the public address and port with a STUN
      binding request to the configured server;
      - TurnAllocation : relay media through a TURN server, over the
      transport of the stream's local binding (UDP, TCP or TLS).

      reflow does not implement ICE.

   @section reflow_security Media Security
      - SRTP keyed through SDP (SDES) : the application gives each stream its
      keys with flowmanager::MediaStream::createOutboundSRTPSession() and
      flowmanager::MediaStream::createInboundSRTPSession().
      - DTLS-SRTP : each flow runs a DTLS handshake on its media port (see
      reflow/dtls_wrapper) and checks the peer's certificate against the
      fingerprint from SDP, set with
      flowmanager::Flow::setRemoteSDPFingerprint(). SRTP keys come from the
      handshake.

      SRTP itself is provided by libsrtp: version 2, or version 1 with the
      CMake option USE_SRTP1.
*/
